{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/thm-grobner-shirshov-basis-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:grobner-shirshov-basis-exists","kind":"theorem","title":"Presentation of the distribution algebra","uses":["papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-non-commutative-formal-group","papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-grobner-shirshov-basis","papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-skewed-poisson-structure"],"cites":["references/leitner2006"],"tags":["groebner-shirshov","presentation","pbw"],"text":"grobner-shirshov-basis-exists.md","leanSource":"grobner-shirshov-basis-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:grobner-shirshov-basis-exists\"></a><p><strong>Proposition</strong> (<span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"leitner2006\">[leitner2006]</span>, Proposition 2.4). With the notation of\nthe <a href=\"#def:grobner-shirshov-basis\" data-at=\"formal-groups-chapter/gs-deformation\">Gröbner basis</a> definition, impose the\ngraded lexicographic ordering on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">TX</code> and let\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I = (f_\\eta \\mid \\eta \\in X) + (g_{\\eta,\\zeta} \\mid \\eta > \\zeta \\in X)</code>. Then\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{f_\\eta, g_{\\eta,\\zeta}\\}</code> is a Gröbner basis of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I</code>, with leading monomials\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\eta^p</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\eta\\zeta</code>, and</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathrm{Dist}(G) \\;\\cong\\; TX / I</code></pre>\n<p>as algebras.</p>\n<p><strong>Theorem</strong> (PBW for splays; <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"leitner2006\">[leitner2006]</span>, Theorem 1.9). Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code> be a\nsplay over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k</code> whose coordinate algebras <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_i</code> have presentations as in\nLemma 1.5 of the paper, let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi</code> be a strongly filtered\n<a href=\"#def:skewed-poisson-structure\" data-at=\"formal-groups-chapter/skewed-poisson\">Poisson structure</a> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code>, and let\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U = T / (fg - gf - \\pi(f, g))</code>. Fixing a total order on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U</code> is\nisomorphic as a <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k</code>-module to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\bigotimes_i A_i</code>.</p>\n<p>For a Lie algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{g} = \\bigoplus_i \\mathfrak{h}_i</code> with abelian\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{h}_i</code>, Theorem 1.9 recovers the usual PBW theorem\n(<span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"leitner2006\">[leitner2006]</span>, Remark 1.10).</p>\n<p>Reference: <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"leitner2006\">[leitner2006]</span>, §§1–2.</p>\n","source":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/grobner-shirshov-basis-exists.md","heading":"Theorem","number":"1.3.2","page":"b/thm-grobner-shirshov-basis-exists","qa":{"counts":{"pass":70,"fail":0,"warn":3,"na":23,"unknown":0,"stale":52}},"lean":{"expected":true,"via":"sibling","path":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/grobner-shirshov-basis-exists.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
